# Append-only ledgers merge by union.
#
# A ledger is written at the BOTTOM and never edited above the last entry, so
# two branches that both append are not really in conflict — they each added
# distinct lines, and the correct resolution is "keep both". `merge=union`
# tells git exactly that, and it turns a hand-resolved conflict into a clean
# auto-merge.
#
# Verified on a real divergence (stele, 3 ahead / 20 behind, add/add on all
# three journal files): with this rule DECISIONS.md auto-merged with zero
# conflict markers and all 20 entries from both sides preserved.
#
# Bottom-appending is what makes this SAFE, not merely tidy. Union merge
# concatenates hunks in file order; with a prepended ledger the result is
# interleaved nonsense, with an appended one it stays chronological.
docs/journal/DECISIONS.md   merge=union

# NOT union, deliberately:
#
#   CHECKPOINT.md  is a projection that gets rewritten, not appended. Union
#                  would duplicate checklist items and resurrect ticked boxes.
#   PLAN.md        is edited in place as phases change.
#   *.golden.json  is generated; regenerate rather than merge.
#
# Both were left conflicting in the verification above, which is the correct
# outcome — the rule discriminates rather than silencing everything.
docs/journal/CHECKPOINT.md  -merge
docs/journal/PLAN.md        -merge
